  "body": "This allows worklets to use their own cache for module fetching, as\ndiscussed in https://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/issues/229 and\nhttps://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/pull/251.\n\n/cc @bfgeek @whatwg/modules \n\nI am a little disturbed by the fact that the \"set up the request\" and \"process the response\" hooks only apply to the top-level fetches, but the \"perform the fetch\" hook applies to every fetch in the tree. I _think_ this is necessary, but if someone could check me on that I'd appreciate it.\n",
